 ],
 "literal": "Of the bards with pot-drums, the chief, / on Atalai hill, in the wide-mouthed deep pool, / along with water-lilies, enfolded wild jasmine, smelling of, your / fragrant forehead, will he forget? Indeed, even though he strives, / many deserts lying across, the rare wealth / is not filled, therefore, delaying is not there today.",
 "translation": "Will he ever forget your fragrant forehead, which smells of wild jasmine enfolded with blue water-lilies from the wide, deep pool on Atalai hill belonging to the chief of bards who play the pot-drum? Even though he strives, the rare wealth he seeks is not yet fully gathered, and many difficult desert paths lie in between; therefore, his delay will not last today.",
 "modern": "பதலை என்னும் வாத்தியத்தை வாசிக்கும் பரிசிலர்களின் தலைவனுடைய அதலை மலையிலுள்ள அகன்ற வாயையுடைய ஆழமான சுனையில் பூத்த குவளைப் பூக்களோடு சேர்த்துத் தொடுத்த காட்டு மல்லிகை மலரின் மணம் வீசும் உன்னுடைய நறிய நெற்றியைத் தலைவன் மறந்துவிடுவானோ? அவன் முயன்றாலும், பல பாலைவனக் கடந்து தேடும் அரிய செல்வம் இன்னும் முழுமையாகக் கிடைக்கவில்லை. அதனால் தான் அவன் தாமதிக்கிறானே தவிர, அவன் உன்னை மறக்கவில்லை; அவன் விரைவில் வந்துவிடுவான்.",
 "explanation": "The friend (thōḻi) is consoling the heroine (thalaivi) who is anxious about the hero's (thalaivaṉ) delay in returning from his quest for wealth. She reassures her that the hero has not forgotten her beautiful, fragrant forehead, which smells of the fresh wild jasmine and water-lilies of the deep pools on Atalai hill. The hill belongs to a generous chief of bards, symbolizing the hero's own noble and loving nature. The friend explains that the only reason for his delay is that the difficult wealth he set out to acquire through arduous desert paths is not yet fully gathered. This poem belongs to the pālai (wasteland) landscape, where the theme of separation and the hardships of the journey to earn wealth are central. Key words like 'naṟunutal' (fragrant forehead) and 'arumporuḷ' (rare wealth) highlight the contrast between the sweet domestic love he left behind and the harsh material duties he must fulfill.",
